       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order. The current FDA-approved label for amlodipine (Norvasc) gives a maximum adult dose of 10 mg once daily. 50 mg is five times that, so it isn't within the labeled maximum. You also haven't given a clinical reason for exceeding it.\n\nI can enter any of these right away:\n- **Amlodipine 5 mg PO once daily**, the usual starting dose.\n- **Amlodipine 10 mg PO once daily**, the labeled maximum.\n- **A different antihypertensive or add-on agent**, if 10 mg isn't enough control.\n\nIf you think a dose above the label is justified, I'd route it through pharmacy and the attending for review. I can also enter the order with a note for that review, but only if the dose is reduced to a label-compliant one. Tell me which option you want and I'll enter it."
